r drop step [tp-tests] \\n\\n[ Edit  ](/root/janusgraph/-/merge_requests/4456/edit \"Edit merge request <kbd class=\\'flat ml-1\\' aria-hidden=true>e</kbd>\")\\n\\nCode \\n\\n  * Review changes \\n  * Check out branch \\n\\n  * [ Open in Web IDE  ](/-/ide/project/root/janusgraph/merge_requests/4456)\\n  * * * *\\n\\n  * Download \\n  * [ Patches  ](/root/janusgraph/-/merge_requests/4456.patch)\\n  * [ Plain diff  ](/root/janusgraph/-/merge_requests/4456.diff)\\n\\n\\n\\nMerge request actions \\n\\n  *     * Notifications \\n\\n  *     * [ Edit  ](/root/janusgraph/-/merge_requests/4456/edit)\\n    * Mark as draft \\n    * Close merge request \\n    * Lock discussion \\n    * Copy reference \\n\\n\\n\\nOpen  Imported  Add batch query support for drop step [tp-tests] \\n\\n[ github/fork/porunov/feature/drop-step-batch-support ](/root/janusgraph/-/tree/github/fork/porunov/feature/drop-step-batch-support \"github/fork/porunov/feature/drop-step-batch-support\") b\" data-clipboard-text=\"github/fork/porunov/feature/drop-step-batch-support\" data-clipboard-handle-tooltip=\"false\" aria-label=\"Copy branch name ` b ` \" aria-live=\"polite\" type=\"button\" class=\"btn js-source-branch-copy gl-mx-1 btn-default btn-sm gl-button btn-default-tertiary btn-icon\" value> into [ master ](/root/janusgraph/-/tree/master \"master\")\\n\\n  * [ Overview  10  ](/root/janusgraph/-/merge_requests/4456)\\n  * [ Commits  1  ](/root/janusgraph/-/merge_requests/4456/commits)\\n  * [ Pipelines  0  ](/root/janusgraph/-/merge_requests/4456/pipelines)\\n  * [ Changes  26  ](/root/janusgraph/-/merge_requests/4456/diffs)\\n\\n\\n\\nMark as done \\n\\nOpen  Imported  [ Administrator  ](/root) requested to merge [ github/fork/porunov/feature/drop-step-batch-support ](/root/janusgraph/-/tree/github/fork/porunov/feature/drop-step-batch-support \"github/fork/porunov/feature/drop-step-batch-support\") into [ master ](/root/janusgraph/-/tree/master \"master\") 1 year ago \\n\\n  * [ Overview  10  ](/root/janusgraph/-/merge_requests/4456)\\n  * [ Commits  1  ](/root/janusgraph/-/merge_requests/4456/commits)\\n  * [ Pipelines  0  ](/root/janusgraph/-/merge_requests/4456/pipelines)\\n  * [ Changes  26  ](/root/janusgraph/-/merge_requests/4456/diffs)\\n\\n\\n\\nMark as done \\n\\nExpand \\n\\n<::after>\\n\\n_Created by: porunov_\\n\\n  * <::marker>Reuse multi-query optimization for TinkerPop ` DropStep `\\n  * <::marker>Change restriction on eligible multi-query traversals and allow multi-query optimizations to be used for queries with steps which contain ` drop() ` step \\n  * <::marker>Add release template for JanusGraph 1.1.0 \\n\\n\\n\\nBenchmarks: \\n    \\n    \\n    CQLMultiQueryDropBenchmark.dropVertices                                                                                       N/A           true                          N/A              5000  avgt    5     98.069 \u00b1   24.496  ms/op\\n    CQLMultiQueryDropBenchmark.dropVertices                                                                                       N/A          false                          N/A              5000  avgt    5   1451.917 \u00b1   90.617  ms/op\\n    CQLMultiQueryDropBenchmark.dropVerticesGremlinQuery                                                                           N/A           true                          N/A              5000  avgt    5    106.444 \u00b1   38.290  ms/op\\n    CQLMultiQueryDropBenchmark.dropVerticesGremlinQuery                                                                           N/A          false                          N/A              5000  avgt    5   1452.070 \u00b1  130.414  ms/op\\n\\nConclusion: same as with direct usage of multi-query the usage of Gremlin ` drop() ` step benefits from re-using multi-query capabilities. Performance of ` drop ` query processing improved more than 13 times. \\n\\nTODO: \\n\\n  * <::marker>Update from ` TinkerPop ` 3.7.3-SNAPSHOT to 3.7.3 when it\\'s released. \\n\\n\\n\\nRelated [ https://github.com/apache/tinkerpop/pull/2609 ](https://github.com/apache/tinkerpop/pull/2609) Related [ https://github.com/apache/tinkerpop/pull/2612 ](https://github.com/apache/tinkerpop/pull/2612)\\n\\n* * *\\n\\nThank you for contributing to JanusGraph! \\n\\nIn order to streamline the review of the contribution we ask you to ensure the following steps have been taken: \\n\\n###  <::after> For all changes: \\n\\n  * Is there an issue associated with this PR? Is it referenced in the commit message? \\n  * Does your PR body contain #xyz where xyz is the issue number you are trying to resolve? \\n  * Has your PR been rebased against the latest commit within the target branch (typically ` master ` )? \\n  * Is your initial contribution a single, squashed commit? \\n\\n\\n\\n###  <::after> For code changes: \\n\\n  * Have you written and/or updated unit tests to verify your changes? \\n  * If adding new dependencies to the code, are these dependencies licensed in a way that is compatible for inclusion under [ ASF 2.0 ](https://www.apache.org/legal/resolved.html#category-a) ? \\n  * If applicable, have you updated the LICENSE.txt file, including the main LICENSE.txt file in the root of this repository? \\n  * If applicable, have you updated the NOTICE.txt file, including the main NOTICE.txt file found in the root of this repository? \\n\\n\\n\\n###  <::after> For documentation related changes: \\n\\n  * Have you ensured that format looks appropriate for the output in which it is rendered? \\n\\n\\n\\n\ud83d\udc4d  0  \ud83d\udc4e  0 \\n\\n##  Merge request reports \\n\\n<::after>\\n\\nApprove \\n\\nApproval is optional  [ ](/help/user/project/merge_requests/approvals/index.md \"About this feature\")\\n\\n<::after>\\n\\n<::before><::after>\\n\\nMerge blocked:  1 check failed \\n\\nMerge conflicts must be resolved. \\n\\n  * Resolve locally \\n  * [ Resolve conflicts  ](/root/janusgraph/-/merge_requests/4456/conflicts)\\n\\n\\n\\nResolve locally  [ Resolve conflicts  ](/root/janusgraph/-/merge_requests/4456/conflicts)\\n\\n<::after>\\n\\nMerge details \\n\\n  * <::marker>The source branch is [ 70 commits behind ](/root/janusgraph/-/commits/master) the target branch. \\n  * <::marker> 1  commit and  1  merge commit will be added to  master  . \\n  * <::marker> Source branch will not be deleted. \\n\\n\\n\\n##  Activity \\n\\nAll activity \\n\\nFilter activity \\n\\nDeselect all \\n\\n  *   *   * Approvals \\n  * Assignees & reviewers \\n  * Comments (from bots) \\n  * Comments (from users) \\n  * Commits & branches \\n  * Edits \\n  * Labels \\n  * Lock status \\n  * Mentions \\n  * Merge request status \\n  * Tracking \\n  *   * \\n\\n\\n<::before>\\n  * [ Administrator  ](/root) added  [ area/core  ](/root/janusgraph/-/merge_requests?label_name=area%2Fcore) [ kind/performance  ](/root/janusgraph/-/merge_requests?label_name=kind%2Fperformance) labels  \u00b7  Imported \\n\\nadded  [ area/core  ](/root/janusgraph/-/merge_requests?label_name=area%2Fcore) [ kind/performance  ](/root/janusgraph/-/merge_requests?label_name=kind%2Fperformance) labels \\n\\n  * [ Administrator  ](/root) changed milestone to [ %Release v1.1.0 ](/root/janusgraph/-/milestones/27) \u00b7  Imported \\n\\nchanged milestone to [ %Release v1.1.0 ](/root/janusgraph/-/milestones/27)\\n\\n  * [ Administrator  ](/root) added  [ cla: external  ](/root/janusgraph/-/merge_requests?label_name=cla%3A+external) label  \u00b7  Imported \\n\\nadded  [ cla: external  ](/root/janusgraph/-/merge_requests?label_name=cla%3A+external) label \\n\\n  * [ ](/root)\\n\\n[ Administrator  ](/root) [ <::before> @root  ](/root) \u00b7  Imported \\n\\nAuthor  Owner \\n\\nMore actions \\n\\n    * Copy link \\n    * Delete comment \\n\\n_Created by: porunov_\\n\\nCurrently I\\'m stuck on the following two TinkerPop tests: \\n    \\n    Error:  Failures: \\n    Error:  org.apache.tinkerpop.gremlin.process.traversal.step.filter.DropTest$Traversals.g_E_propertiesXweightX_drop\\n    Error:    Run 1: DropTest$Traversals>DropTest.g_E_propertiesXweightX_drop:98->DropTest.lambda$g_E_propertiesXweightX_drop$1:98 expected:<0> but was:<1>\\n    Error:    Run 2: DropTest$Traversals>DropTest.g_E_propertiesXweightX_drop:98->DropTest.lambda$g_E_propertiesXweightX_drop$1:98 expected:<0> but was:<1>\\n    [INFO] \\n    Error:  org.apache.tinkerpop.gremlin.process.traversal.step.filter.DropTest$Traversals.g_V_properties_propertiesXstartTimeX_drop\\n    Error:    Run 1: DropTest$Traversals>DropTest.g_V_properties_propertiesXstartTimeX_drop:109->DropTest.lambda$g_V_properties_propertiesXstartTimeX_drop$3:109 expected:<0> but was:<1>\\n    Error:    Run 2: DropTest$Traversals>DropTest.g_V_properties_propertiesXstartTimeX_drop:109->DropTest.lambda$g_V_properties_propertiesXstartTimeX_drop$3:109 expected:<0> but was:<2>\\n\\nThe first test checks that ` drop() ` works for Edge properties. The second one checks that ` drop() ` works for meta properties. For some reason those two TinkerPop tests are failing with this PR. However, I verified that the removal operation works in this PR by adding ` testMetaPropertiesDrop ` and ` testEdgePropertiesDrop ` tests (similarly as in those TinkerPop tests). It can be seen that these added tests are passing. For now the reason for these two TinkerPop tests to fail is unknown to me. Additional pair of eyes would me much appreciated. \\n\\nTinkerPop tests for inmemory database can be triggered with: \\n    \\n    mvn clean install --projects janusgraph-inmemory -DskipTests=true --batch-mode --also-make\\n    \\n    mvn verify --projects janusgraph-inmemory -Dtest.skip.tp=false -Dtest=org.janusgraph.blueprints.inmemory.process.InMemoryMultiQueryJanusGraphProcessTest -pl janusgraph-inmemory\\n\\n_By Administrator on 2024-05-17T22:15:29_\\n\\n  * [ ](/root)\\n\\n[ Administrator  ](/root) [ <::before> @root  ](/root) \u00b7  Imported \\n\\nAuthor  Owner \\n\\nMore actions \\n\\n    * Copy link \\n    * Delete comment \\n\\n_Created by: porunov_\\n\\nOne of the observations is that if I change the default barrier step size from the default ` 2500 ` to ` 1 ` ( ` query.batch.limited-size=1 ` ) then all tests passes. I.e. it means that the fact that we store those properties in the barrier before we actually remove them changes the result of those two tests. \\n\\n_By Administrator on 2024-05-17T22:37:52_\\n\\n  * [ ](/root)\\n\\n[ Administrator  ](/root) [ <::before> @root  ](/root) \u00b7  Imported \\n\\nAuthor  Owner \\n\\nMore actions \\n\\n    * Copy link \\n    * Delete comment \\n\\n_Created by: ntisseyre_\\n\\n> Currently I\\'m stuck on the following two TinkerPop tests: \\n>     \\n>     Error:  Failures: \\n>     Error:  org.apache.tinkerpop.gremlin.process.traversal.step.filter.DropTest$Traversals.g_E_propertiesXweightX_drop\\n>     Error:    Run 1: DropTest$Traversals>DropTest.g_E_propertiesXweightX_drop:98->DropTest.lambda$g_E_propertiesXweightX_drop$1:98 expected:<0> but was:<1>\\n>     Error:    Run 2: DropTest$Traversals>DropTest.g_E_propertiesXweightX_drop:98->DropTest.lambda$g_E_propertiesXweightX_drop$1:98 expected:<0> but was:<1>\\n>     [INFO] \\n>     Error:  org.apache.tinkerpop.gremlin.process.traversal.step.filter.DropTest$Traversals.g_V_properties_propertiesXstartTimeX_drop\\n>     Error:    Run 1: DropTest$Traversals>DropTest.g_V_properties_propertiesXstartTimeX_drop:109->DropTest.lambda$g_V_properties_propertiesXstartTimeX_drop$3:109 expected:<0> but was:<1>\\n>     Error:    Run 2: DropTest$Traversals>DropTest.g_V_properties_propertiesXstartTimeX_drop:109->DropTest.lambda$g_V_properties_propertiesXstartTimeX_drop$3:109 expected:<0> but was:<2>\\n> \\n> The first test checks that ` drop() ` works for Edge properties. The second one checks that ` drop() ` works for meta properties. For some reason those two TinkerPop tests are failing with this PR. However, I verified that the removal operation works in this PR by adding ` testMetaPropertiesDrop ` and ` testEdgePropertiesDrop ` tests (similarly as in those TinkerPop tests). It can be seen that these added tests are passing. For now the reason for these two TinkerPop tests to fail is unknown to me. Additional pair of eyes would me much appreciated. \\n> \\n> TinkerPop tests for inmemory database can be triggered with: \\n>     \\n>     mvn clean install --projects janusgraph-inmemory -DskipTests=true --batch-mode --also-make\\n>     \\n>     mvn verify --projects janusgraph-inmemory -Dtest.skip.tp=false -Dtest=org.janusgraph.blueprints.inmemory.process.InMemoryMultiQueryJanusGraphProcessTest -pl janusgraph-inmemory\\n\\nI noticed, I am not sure if it is related, but you might have missed adding ` JanusGraphDropStep ` here: [ https://github.com/JanusGraph/janusgraph/blob/a2e3521d28de37ca01d08166777d77c0943a9db5/janusgraph-backend-testutils/src/main/java/org/janusgraph/graphdb/database/LazyLoadGraphTest.java#L40 ](https://github.com/JanusGraph/janusgraph/blob/a2e3521d28de37ca01d08166777d77c0943a9db5/janusgraph-backend-testutils/src/main/java/org/janusgraph/graphdb/database/LazyLoadGraphTest.java#L40)\\n\\n_By Administrator on 2024-05-17T22:39:02_\\n\\n  * [ ](/root)\\n\\n[ Administrator  ](/root) [ <::before> @root  ](/root) \u00b7  Imported \\n\\nAuthor  Owner \\n\\nMore actions \\n\\n    * Copy link \\n    * Delete comment \\n\\n_Created by: porunov_\\n\\n> I noticed, I am not sure if it is related, but you might have missed adding JanusGraphDropStep here: \\n\\n` JanusGraphDropStep ` is replaced as part of ` JanusGraphLocalQueryOptimizerStrategy ` . So I believe it should be fine. I feels that those two TinkerPop tests don\\'t like that I\\'m storing properties for removal in the barrier step for some reason. However, I can\\'t figure out \"why\" yet. \\n\\n_By Administrator on 2024-05-17T22:43:42_\\n\\n  * [ ](/root)\\n\\n[ Administrator  ](/root) [ <::before> @root  ](/root) \u00b7  Imported \\n\\nAuthor  Owner \\n\\nMore actions \\n\\n    * Copy link \\n    * Delete comment \\n\\n_Created by: porunov_\\n\\nAfter a bit of debugging I found the root cause of the problem. When removing Edge properties I see that each edge property is wrapped into ` B_O_Traverser ` which is passed to ` NoOpBarrier ` step. That traverser is added to the ` TraverserSet ` [ here ](https://github.com/apache/tinkerpop/blob/459f32cfe33cd0b68b68f9dff3fad04609904407/gremlin-core/src/main/java/org/apache/tinkerpop/gremlin/process/traversal/step/map/NoOpBarrierStep.java#L70) . After I loaded the same graph as in TinkerPop tests locally I noticed that 4 out of 6 edge properties were removed, but 2 didn\\'t because they were considered the \"same\" properties as were already added into the ` TraverserSet ` (thus their Traverser\\'s merged). The root cause is that ` relation ` is not checked on equality for ` SimpleJanusGraphProperty ` . This bug was introduced 9 years ago here: [ https://github.com/JanusGraph/janusgraph/commit/795d7b0131c1e62fdf354e0a8e4718d6627f1418 ](https://github.com/JanusGraph/janusgraph/commit/795d7b0131c1e62fdf354e0a8e4718d6627f1418)\\n\\nThe fix should be a simple one and I will add a separate test case with ` barrier() ` \\\\+ ` drop() ` of edge properties with the same ` key ` and ` value ` . \\n\\n_By Administrator on 2024-05-18T01:08:11_\\n\\n  * [ ](/root)\\n\\n[ Administrator  ](/root) [ <::before> @root  ](/root) \u00b7  Imported \\n\\nAuthor  Owner \\n\\nMore actions \\n\\n    * Copy link \\n    * Delete comment \\n\\n_Created by: porunov_\\n\\n> After a bit of debugging I found the root cause of the problem. When removing Edge properties I see that each edge property is wrapped into ` B_O_Traverser ` which is passed to ` NoOpBarrier ` step. That traverser is added to the ` TraverserSet ` [ here ](https://github.com/apache/tinkerpop/blob/459f32cfe33cd0b68b68f9dff3fad04609904407/gremlin-core/src/main/java/org/apache/tinkerpop/gremlin/process/traversal/step/map/NoOpBarrierStep.java#L70) . After I loaded the same graph as in TinkerPop tests locally I noticed that 4 out of 6 edge properties were removed, but 2 didn\\'t because they were considered the \"same\" properties as were already added into the ` TraverserSet ` (thus their Traverser\\'s merged). The root cause is that ` relation ` is not checked on equality for ` SimpleJanusGraphProperty ` . This bug was introduced 9 years ago here: [ 795d7b0 ](https://github.com/JanusGraph/janusgraph/commit/795d7b0131c1e62fdf354e0a8e4718d6627f1418)\\n> \\n> The fix should be a simple one and I will add a separate test case with ` barrier() ` \\\\+ ` drop() ` of edge properties with the same ` key ` and ` value ` . \\n\\nHuh. Seems I was a bit wrong. If I fix that ` drop ` tests then ` dedup ` tests start to fail. Hmm. Now I\\'m confused where the fix should happen. \\n\\n_By Administrator on 2024-05-18T01:34:37_\\n\\n> The fix should be a simple one and I will add a separate test case with `barrier()` + `drop()` of edge properties with the same `key` and `value`. Huh. Seems I was a bit wrong. If I fix that `drop` tests then `dedup` tests start to fail. Hmm. Now I\\'m confused where the fix should happen. *By Administrator on 2024-05-18T01:34:37*\">\\n\\n  * [ ](/root)\\n\\n[ Administrator  ](/root) [ <::before> @root  ](/root) \u00b7  Imported \\n\\nAuthor  Owner \\n\\nMore actions \\n\\n    * Copy link \\n    * Delete comment \\n\\n_Created by: porunov_\\n\\nSeems I\\'m missing how ` barrier ` step suppose to work. It could be that we actually don\\'t have any bug which I described above and it\\'s actually intended to be like that (at least I verified that the behavior is consistent between TinkerGraph and JanusGraph, so I guess we are fine there). However, I think it makes sense to double check with the TinkerPop community regrading ` barrier ` and ` dedup ` behavior. Thus, I opened a thread here: [ https://discord.com/channels/838910279550238720/1241219665376706603 ](https://discord.com/channels/838910279550238720/1241219665376706603)\\n\\nIf that is confirmed to be the intended behavior then I will try to think about a bit different solution. \\n\\n_By Administrator on 2024-05-18T02:52:43_\\n\\n  * [ ](/root)\\n\\n[ Administrator  ](/root) [ <::before> @root  ](/root) \u00b7  Imported \\n\\nAuthor  Owner \\n\\nMore actions \\n\\n    * Copy link \\n    * Delete comment \\n\\n_Created by: porunov_\\n\\nOne of the potential solutions is to make out own ` NoOpBarrierStep ` which skips anything except ` Vertex ` and insert that barrier step as part of multi-query optimization instead of the standard ` NoOpBarrierStep ` . However, there are many places in code logic where we need to check and sometimes cast a step to ` NoOpBarrierStep ` . It would make sense to extend ` NoOpBarrierStep ` and overwrite part of the logic, but ` NoOpBarrierStep ` is currently ` final ` and the necessary properties are ` private ` which makes things a bit challenging. Potentially, when the following PR is merged and the next TinkerPop version is released it should be easier to extend logic: [ https://github.com/apache/tinkerpop/pull/2612 ](https://github.com/apache/tinkerpop/pull/2612)\\n\\n_By Administrator on 2024-05-18T15:14:34_\\n\\n  * [ Administrator  ](/root) mentioned in merge request [ !2612 (closed) ](/root/janusgraph/-/merge_requests/2612 \"Bump bigtable-hbase-2.x-shaded from 1.16.0 to 1.20.0\") \u00b7  Imported \\n\\nmentioned in merge request [ !2612 (closed) ](/root/janusgraph/-/merge_requests/2612 \"Bump bigtable-hbase-2.x-shaded from 1.16.0 to 1.20.0\")\\n\\n_By Administrator on 2024-08-29T07:26:45_\\n\\n  * [ ](/root)\\n\\n[ Administrator  ](/root) [ <::before> @root  ](/root) \u00b7  Imported \\n\\nAuthor  Owner \\n\\nMore actions \\n\\n    * Copy link \\n    * Delete comment \\n\\n_Created by: porunov_\\n\\nBoth TinkerPop PRs are now merged ( [ https://github.com/apache/tinkerpop/pull/2612 ](https://github.com/apache/tinkerpop/pull/2612) and [ https://github.com/apache/tinkerpop/pull/2609 ](https://github.com/apache/tinkerpop/pull/2609) ). This will allow us to extend ` NoOpBarrierStep ` to skip everything except vertices. Thus should be also an improvement by itself because there is no reason for multi-query strategy to inject ` barrier ` steps which trigger batching for anything except edges because we multi-query step registers ` Vertices ` only as for now, and thus anything else is just a potential waist of operations. When we replace it with our own barrier step it will allow us: \\n\\n    * <::marker>Safely open multi-query strategy for ` drop() ` step. \\n    * <::marker>Slightly improve processing of edges / properties / meta properties because they won\\'t be affected by the barrier anymore (i.e. a bit less of unnecessary operations). \\n\\nNow we need to wait for TinkerPop 3.7.3 to proceed without doing major hacks. \\n\\n_By Administrator on 2024-05-24T17:10:45_\\n\\n  * [ Administrator  ](/root) requested review from [ @root ](/root \"Administrator\") \u00b7  Imported \\n\\nrequested review from [ @root ](/root \"Administrator\")\\n\\n_By Administrator on 2024-06-01T08:52:01_\\n\\n  * [ ](/root)\\n\\n[ Administrator  ](/root) [ <::before> @root  ](/root) \u00b7  Imported \\n\\nAuthor  Owner \\n\\nMore actions \\n\\n    * Copy link \\n    * Delete comment \\n\\n_Created by: porunov_\\n\\nThe PR is now ready for the review. All tests passed as can be seen from my branch ( [ here ](https://github.com/porunov/janusgraph/commit/7429b5f94aa95c79a35c70d2baa70626a0159722) ). \\n\\nNotes: \\n\\n    * <::marker>This PR is using TinkerPop 3.7.3-SNAPSHOT. Thus, we can\\'t merge it until TinkerPop 3.7.3 is released. \\n    * <::marker>The attached link to my branch shows that all tests (including tp-tests) passed. However, if berkeleydb tp-tests fail for this PR - it\\'s not related to this PR. We currently have flaky berkeleydb configuration in ` master ` branch which makes tp-tests for berkeleydb fail often. This problem appeared after merging the following PR #4425 . \\n\\n_By Administrator on 2024-06-01T08:59:12