\\n\\n## Steps:\\n\\n### 1. Identify Merge Requests for Release\\n- Navigate to the project\\'s Merge Requests page\\n- Filter by milestone (e.g., \"Release v1.1.0\")\\n- Review the list of open merge requests\\n\\n### 2. Assess Merge Request Status\\nFor each merge request:\\n- Check if it\\'s \"Ready to merge\" (green checkmark)\\n- Verify there are no merge conflicts\\n- Ensure the source branch is not too far behind target branch\\n- Review any required approvals or checks\\n\\n### 3. Merge Ready Requests\\n- Click on the merge request to open details\\n- Verify all checks pass (CI/CD pipelines, approvals)\\n- Click the \"Merge\" button\\n- Wait for confirmation that merge is complete\\n- Verify pipeline is triggered automatically\\n\\n### 4. Handle Blocked Requests\\nFor merge requests that are blocked:\\n- Identify the blocking issue (merge conflicts, failing tests, etc.)\\n- Document the specific problem in team communication\\n- Create action plan for resolution\\n- Assign responsible team members if needed\\n\\n### 5. Team Communication\\n- Use RocketChat to communicate status updates\\n- Share which merge requests were successfully merged\\n- Report on blocked requests and next steps\\n- Coordinate team sync for complex issues\\n\\n## Best Practices:\\n- Always merge dependency updates first (like dependabot PRs)\\n- Document merge decisions and rationale\\n- Keep team informed of progress\\n- Schedule follow-ups for blocked items\\n- Verify pipelines complete successfully after merges\\n\\n## Example Workflow:\\n1. Filter merge requests by milestone \"Release v1.1.0\"\\n2. Merge !4657 (dependency update) - ready to merge\\n3. Document !4456 as blocked - needs conflict resolution\\n4. Communicate status to team via RocketChat\\n5. Schedule team sync for blocked items\\n'}, thought='Perfect! Now let me save this successful workflow as an SOP for future reference. This will help streamline the process for reviewing and merging merge requests for future releases:', action=<ActionType.MCP: 'call_tool_mcp'>, security_risk=None), MCPObservation(content='{\"meta\": null, \"content\": [{\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": \"Successfully saved new guide \\'ReviewAndMergeReleaseMergeRequests\\' for platform \\'GitLab\\'.\", \"annotations\": null}], \"isError\": false}', observation=<ObservationType.MCP: 'mcp'>, name='update_operation_guide', arguments={'platform': 'GitLab', 'operation': 'ReviewAndMergeReleaseMergeRequests', 'details': '# GitLab - Review and Merge Release Merge Requests\\n\\n## Overview\\nThis SOP outlines the process for reviewing, managing, and merging merge requests assigned to a specific release milestone in GitLab.\\n\\n## Steps:\\n\\n### 1. Identify Merge Requests for Release\\n- Navigate to the project\\'s Merge Requests page\\n- Filter by milestone (e.g., \"Release v1.1.0\")\\n- Review the list of open merge requests\\n\\n### 2. Assess Merge Request Status\\nFor each merge request:\\n- Check if it\\'s \"Ready to merge\" (green checkmark)\\n- Verify there are no merge conflicts\\n- Ensure the source branch is not too far behind target branch\\n- Review any required approvals or checks\\n\\n### 3. Merge Ready Requests\\n- Click on the merge request to open details\\n- Verify all checks pass (CI/CD pipelines, approvals)\\n- Click the \"Merge\" button\\n- Wait for confirmation that merge is complete\\n- Verify pipeline is triggered automatically\\n\\n### 4. Handle Blocked Requests\\nFor merge requests that are blocked:\\n- Identify the blocking issue (merge conflicts, failing tests, etc.)\\n- Document the specific problem in team communication\\n- Create action plan for resolution\\n- Assign responsible team members if needed\\n\\n### 5. Team Communication\\n- Use RocketChat to communicate status updates\\n- Share which merge requests were successfully merged\\n- Report on blocked requests and next steps\\n- Coordinate team sync for complex issues\\n\\n## Best Practices:\\n- Always merge dependency updates first (like dependabot PRs)\\n- Document merge decisions and rationale\\n- Keep team informed of progress\\n- Schedule follow-ups for blocked items\\n- Verify pipelines complete successfully after merges\\n\\n## Example Workflow:\\n1. Filter merge requests by milestone \"Release v1.1.0\"\\n2. Merge !4657 (dependency update) - ready to merge\\n3. Document !4456 as blocked - needs conflict resolution\\n4. Communicate status to team via RocketChat\\n5. Schedule team sync for blocked items\\n'}), MCPAction(name='update_operation_guide', arguments={'platform': 'RocketChat', 'operation': 'TeamStatusUpdateForMergeRequests', 'details': '\\n# RocketChat - Team Status Update for Merge Requests\\n\\n## Overview\\nThis SOP outlines how to effectively communicate merge request status updates and coordinate team discussions in RocketChat.\\n\\n## Steps:\\n\\n### 1. Access the Team Channel\\n- Navigate to RocketChat at http://the-agent-company.com:3000/home\\n- Click on the relevant team channel (e.g., \"Janusgraph\")\\n- Wait for the channel to load\\n\\n### 2. Send Initial Status Report\\n- Use clear formatting with emojis and bullet points\\n- Include:\\n  - \u2705 Ready to merge requests with links\\n  - \u274c Blocked requests with specific issues\\n  - Meeting agenda proposal\\n  - Request for team availability\\n\\n### 3. Send Progress Updates\\n- After completing actions (merges, etc.)\\n- Use \u2705 emoji for completed items\\n- Include next steps clearly\\n- Reference specific merge request numbers\\n\\n### 4. Coordinate Team Sync\\n- Propose specific agenda items\\n- Request availability from team members\\n- Follow up if no immediate response\\n\\n## Message Templates:\\n\\n### Initial Status Report:\\n```\\nHi team! I\\'ve reviewed the open merge requests for milestone [Milestone Name]. Here\\'s the current status:\\n\\n\u2705 **Ready to Merge:**\\n\u2022 [!4657](link) - \"[Title]\" - [Brief description]\\n\\n\u274c **Blocked:**\\n\u2022 [!4456](link) - \"[Title]\" - [Specific blocking issue]\\n\\n**Meeting Agenda Proposal:**\\n1. Review and merge ready requests\\n2. Discuss resolution for blocked items\\n3. [Additional agenda items]\\n\\nWhen would be a good time to schedule a quick sync?\\n```\\n\\n### Progress Update:\\n```\\n\u2705 **UPDATE**: Successfully merged [!4657](link) into master!\\n\\n**Current Status:**\\n\u2705 Merged: [!4657](link) - [Description]\\n\u274c Blocked: [!4456](link) - [Blocking issue]\\n\\n**Next Steps:**\\n1. [Action item 1]\\n2. [Action item 2]\\n3. [Action item 3]\\n\\nLet me know when you\\'re available to discuss the blocked items!\\n```\\n\\n## Best Practices:\\n- Always include direct links to merge requests\\n- Use clear emoji indicators (\u2705 for done, \u274c for blocked)\\n- Keep messages concise but informative\\n- Follow up if team members don\\'t respond\\n- Document decisions made in team discussions\\n\\n'}, thought='Excellent! Now let me also save an SOP for the RocketChat communication part of this workflow:', action=<ActionType.MCP: 'call_tool_mcp'>, security_risk=None), MCPObservation(content='{\"meta\": null, \"content\": [{\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": \"Successfully saved new guide \\'TeamStatusUpdateForMergeRequests\\' for platform \\'RocketChat\\'.\", \"annotations\": null}], \"isError\": false}', observation=<ObservationType.MCP: 'mcp'>, name='update_operation_guide', arguments={'platform': 'RocketChat', 'operation': 'TeamStatusUpdateForMergeRequests', 'details': '\\n# RocketChat - Team Status Update for Merge Requests\\n\\n## Overview\\nThis SOP outlines how to effectively communicate merge request status updates and coordinate team discussions in RocketChat.\\n\\n## Steps:\\n\\n### 1. Access the Team Channel\\n- Navigate to RocketChat at http://the-agent-company.com:3000/home\\n- Click on the relevant team channel (e.g., \"Janusgraph\")\\n- Wait for the channel to load\\n\\n### 2. Send Initial Status Report\\n- Use clear formatting with emojis and bullet points\\n- Include:\\n